    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds pretty strict. I'm worried that if we just ban everything, we might actually hurt our inclusivity goals. Some employees feel like being able to speak up about social justice issues or certain policies is a key part of feeling seen and included at work. Wouldn't banning those discussions basically silence the very people we're trying to support? How would you justify that to the employees who think silence equals complicity?",
